@startuml STM-3_ChargingPillar
!include _style.iuml
title STM-3 ChargingPillar lifecycle · v0.3 (ADR-0016) · 25/10/2026 · #1–#3 in code (PillarLifecyclePolicy, PR 33)\ncharge_points.lifecycle (administrative only) · connectivity online/offline is a separate attribute (T61, Trí)
[*] --> registered : Admin adds serial to registry
registered --> awaiting_connection : Operator onboards\n/ issue credential
awaiting_connection --> in_service : first accepted connection\n(BootNotification)
in_service --> disabled : Operator takes pillar out of service\n/ hide from search
disabled --> in_service : Operator returns pillar to service
disabled --> decommissioned : Admin retires device
decommissioned --> [*]
note bottom
  Connectivity (not a lifecycle state): is_online + last_seen_at,
  set by ocpp-gateway on connect / socket close / ping timeout.
  A disabled pillar can still be online; an in_service pillar can be offline.
  Offline alert (FaultEvent) is raised after the alert delay, ≤ 900 s (F-10).
end note
@enduml